------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party software invoked as subprocesses
------------------------------------------------------------------------

senex shells out to several third-party tools at runtime. These tools are
not bundled or redistributed by senex; users install them separately.
Their licenses are listed here for transparency. Subprocess invocation
does not contaminate senex's own Apache-2.0 license.

  * SGLang
      Source: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang
      License: Apache License, Version 2.0
      Used by senex as the default local inference server (OpenAI-compat
      API on localhost). Invoked via Docker Compose
      (senex/infra/sglang/).

  * GitNexus
      Source: https://github.com/parthalon025/gitnexus
      License: PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0
      Used by senex as an optional code-graph context provider. Invoked
      via `npx gitnexus` subprocess. NOTE: PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0
      restricts commercial use of GitNexus itself; commercial users of
      senex who also wish to use GitNexus must obtain a separate
      commercial license from the GitNexus maintainer. senex's own
      Apache-2.0 license is not affected by this dependency because
      GitNexus is invoked as an out-of-process tool and is not bundled.

  * semgrep
      Source: https://github.com/semgrep/semgrep
      License: GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1 (LGPL-2.1)
      Used by senex as an optional static-analysis tool invoked via
      subprocess. LGPL-2.1 obligations are limited to the semgrep
      binary itself; senex does not link against semgrep code.

